    "judge_text": "**Indicator Compliance:**\nThe code uses RSI (not Williams %R) and omits the Momentum indicator entirely, replacing it with a simple price direction check (`close[0] > close[-1]`). The assignment explicitly requires `bt.indicators.WilliamsR` and `bt.indicators.Momentum` \u2014 neither appears in the code.\n\n**Problem Solving:**\nThe core entry logic is fundamentally different: the assignment requires Williams %R crossovers at -80 (long) and -20 (short) combined with Momentum sign, but the code uses RSI crossovers at 30/70 levels. While RSI and Williams %R are conceptually related oscillators, the specific crossover levels, directional logic, and Momentum confirmation are all absent \u2014 this is not a simplification of the same idea, it is a different strategy.\n\n**Relevance:**\nThe code does implement the structural skeleton correctly (long/short trading, ATR-based protective stop, `trailing_stop` parameter, exit on opposite signal), which shows the assignment was partially read. However, substituting both specified entry indicators with an unrelated indicator (RSI) without any justification goes beyond acceptable simplification and changes the core logic of the strategy.\n\nRating: [[0]]"
